## PR Title
Connect reset signal to fix issue of XXXXXXX in RISCOF

## PR Description
Connects the previously unwired `reset` to the Register File so that x0 is initialised correctly, fixing an X-propagation problem observed in RISCOF runs. Per the conversation, the testbench was reworked so it doesn't try to write to x0 directly but instead asserts and the RegisterFile enforces x0=0.

## PR Comments
**TheDeepestSpace** (Oct 3, 2025): "The `nop` testbench is failing because its using `x0` register which is supposed to always be zero. Since now the `reset` signal is passed to RF module properly, `x0` gets correctly initialized to zero and testbench overwrites the value, which we should not do."

**RunzeZhu28** (Oct 3, 2025): "I keep the tb to write to x0 but change the assert and modify the RegisterFile to ensure x0 is always 0. Now all passed"

